course: dictionary
lesson: 10156
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is meant. The word thumb is a good example. «The tripod grip holds the pencil between thumb and first finger» uses thumb as a body part: the short, thick finger on the side of your hand.
explain: Thumb can also be an action word. «Thumb through a book» means to turn the pages quickly. In «Count on your fingers this way, thumb 1, next finger 2», thumb is a label for a number, so the sentence is about counting.
explain: Ask yourself: does this fit a body part, an action, or a phrase? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Thumb is a noun (a thumb, thumbs) and a verb (thumb, thumbs, thumbed, thumbing).
fact: «Thumb» means the short, thick finger on the side of your hand.
fact: As a verb, «thumb» means to turn pages quickly, as in «thumb through a book».
fact: «Thumbs up» means good or yes; «thumbs down» means bad or no. «Rule of thumb» means a rough, practical rule.
fact: The thumb is opposable: it can touch the other fingers, which helps humans grip and use tools.
exercise: «The tripod grip holds the pencil between thumb and first finger.» What is the thumb here? | A tool for turning pages | *A short, thick finger on the side of your hand | A kind of pencil | A rough rule
exercise: Ana says, «I will thumb through the atlas to find Peru.» What does thumb mean? | To press a button with a finger | To hold something tightly | *To turn the pages quickly | To count on your fingers
exercise: Your teacher gives the class a «thumbs up». What does it mean? | Go outside for break | *Good or yes | Stop and wait | Bad or no
test: Why is the thumb so useful for holding things? | It is the longest finger on the hand | It is always kept folded away | *It can touch the other fingers, which helps the hand grip | It helps you hear better
test: «Rule of thumb» is a phrase. What does it mean? | *A rough, practical rule | A rule about thumbs only | A rule for measuring things exactly | A very strict law
exam: «Some apps are designed to keep you scrolling, so noticing how you feel in the thumbs and wrists is a smart signal to stop.» What does thumbs mean here? | Good or yes | To turn pages quickly | *The short, thick fingers on your hands | A rough, practical rule
